    {
      "id": 39520,
      "name": "Spiff",
      "username": "Spiff",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/spiff/{size}/1865_2.png",
      "created_at": "2012-09-29T21:57:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>In the contexts in which you see that text the most, it means this:</p><p>Each turn (meaning, the villain turn, the environment turn, or each one of the hero turns), the first time something happens, do what the card says to do. &nbsp;If it happens again during the same turn, don't trigger it again, but if it happens again on a following turn, you should trigger it.</p><p>For example, \"the first time this card takes damage each turn, do XYZ\" means that if Haka plays a one-shot that damages the card, XYZ will happen. &nbsp;But if Haka then activates a power on that same turn that also does damage, XYZ is not triggered. &nbsp;However, when it's the next hero's turn, you'll be checking for the first time the card takes damage again.</p><p>A round is a full trip around the table (villain, all heroes, environment). &nbsp;A turn is each part of that.</p><p>Hope that makes sense.</p>",
      "post_number": 2,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T02:13:15.306Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
