      "raw": "<p>In the contexts in which you see that text the most, it means this:</p><p>Each turn (meaning, the villain turn, the environment turn, or each one of the hero turns), the first time something happens, do what the card says to do. &nbsp;If it happens again during the same turn, don&#39;t trigger it again, but if it happens again on a following turn, you should trigger it.</p><p>For example, &quot;the first time this card takes damage each turn, do XYZ&quot; means that if Haka plays a one-shot that damages the card, XYZ will happen. &nbsp;But if Haka then activates a power on that same turn that also does damage, XYZ is not triggered. &nbsp;However, when it&#39;s the next hero&#39;s turn, you&#39;ll be checking for the first time the card takes damage again.</p><p>A round is a full trip around the table (villain, all heroes, environment). &nbsp;A turn is each part of that.</p><p>Hope that makes sense.</p>",
